From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal/drivers/qcom/tsens: Fix threshold codes for negative results

degc_to_code() does its arithmetic in u64. When degc * slope + offset is
negative, which happens for the -40 C lower bound that tsens_set_trips()
uses below the first trip on a sensor with a small 30 C calibration
code, the value wraps and is clamped to THRESHOLD_MAX_ADC_CODE. The lower
threshold then sits above the current temperature and the lower-threshold
status is permanently asserted. Do the computation in s64 and clamp to the
width of the sensor's code field (8 bits on MSM8960/APQ8064, where 0x3ff
would otherwise be truncated by the regmap field write).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c	2026-11-16 02:41:38.095835310 +0100
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c	2026-11-16 02:42:36.819014701 +0100
@@ -290,10 +290,19 @@
 
 static inline u32 degc_to_code(int degc, const struct tsens_sensor *s)
 {
-	u64 code = div_u64(((u64)degc * s->slope + s->offset), SLOPE_FACTOR);
+	const struct reg_field *f = &s->priv->fields[LAST_TEMP_0];
+	s64 max_code = min_t(s64, THRESHOLD_MAX_ADC_CODE,
+			     GENMASK(f->msb - f->lsb, 0));
+	/*
+	 * degc and the result can be negative (e.g. the -40 C lower trip
+	 * clamp on a sensor whose 30 C calibration code is small). Doing this
+	 * in u64 wraps around and clamps to the maximum code, which puts the
+	 * lower threshold above the current temperature.
+	 */
+	s64 code = div_s64((s64)degc * s->slope + s->offset, SLOPE_FACTOR);
 
-	pr_debug("%s: raw_code: 0x%llx, degc:%d\n", __func__, code, degc);
-	return clamp_val(code, THRESHOLD_MIN_ADC_CODE, THRESHOLD_MAX_ADC_CODE);
+	pr_debug("%s: raw_code: %lld, degc:%d\n", __func__, code, degc);
+	return clamp_val(code, THRESHOLD_MIN_ADC_CODE, max_code);
 }
 
 static inline int code_to_degc(u32 adc_code, const struct tsens_sensor *s)
